#chrom	start	end	gene
# GRCh38 coordinates for the melanoma_genes.tsv driver-gene seed list, resolved 2026-08-30 via
# Ensembl's REST API (https://rest.ensembl.org/lookup/symbol/homo_sapiens/<GENE>?content-type=application/json),
# not guessed -- each lookup's assembly_name was confirmed "GRCh38" before use. Coordinates below
# are the Ensembl gene span (1-based inclusive, as Ensembl reports it) converted to standard BED
# (0-based, half-open: bed_start = ensembl_start - 1, bed_end = ensembl_end unchanged), then padded
# +/-2000bp on both ends per the TODO note in melanoma_genes.tsv ("+/- flanking region").
#
# TERT note: TERT is minus-strand (chr5:1,253,147-1,295,086), so its promoter -- where the
# well-known recurrent C228T/C250T hotspot mutations sit -- lies just upstream of the gene's
# high-coordinate end (1,295,086), not the low-coordinate start. Rather than assert an exact
# hotspot coordinate from memory (unverified), the uniform 2000bp padding is relied on to
# comfortably cover the promoter region without pinpointing it -- if precise hotspot-level
# resolution is ever needed, verify the exact positions independently before trusting them.
#
# Sequence-name convention: "chr"-prefixed to match Homo_sapiens_assembly38.fasta (Broad's GATK
# bundle, see docs/data_sources.md §2) -- Ensembl's own API returns bare chromosome numbers.
#
# Scope note (Phase 2): unlike modules/alignment.nf (which ignores interval_list entirely --
# see nextflow.config's dev-profile comment), Mutect2 and GetPileupSummaries DO respect -L, so
# this file is what actually makes the Phase 2 dev-profile smoke test fast. IMPORTANT CAVEAT --
# see docs/PHASE2_NOTES.md: the current dev-profile BAMs are built from a 10,000-read-pair
# subsample taken randomly across the WHOLE genome (docs/PHASE1_NOTES.md), so there is no reason
# to expect any of those reads happen to fall within these specific gene windows. Restricting to
# this BED validates that the Mutect2/contamination DAG and containers run correctly -- it does
# NOT validate real variant-calling behaviour at these loci until real full-depth coverage exists.
chr1	114702467	114718775	NRAS
chr4	54655266	54742783	KIT
chr5	1251146	1297086	TERT
chr7	140717326	140927199	BRAF
chr9	21964923	21997301	CDKN2A
chr10	87860637	87973930	PTEN
chr17	7659778	7689546	TP53
chr17	31092882	31384116	NF1
